BS_:

BU_: ADAS CLU DATC ICSC MCU RR VCMS VCU Vector__XXX WHL YRS

BA_DEF_ BO_  "VFrameFormat" ENUM  "StandardCAN","ExtendedCAN";
BA_DEF_DEF_ "VFrameFormat" "StandardCAN";

CM_ "GV60 (CCU CAN hub) frame ids. The CCU hub, which replaced the older ICU CAN hub, re-addresses classic 11-bit car-bus frames onto 29-bit extended ids that encode the original 11-bit id. This predates ccNC head units and is NOT a ccNC feature:";
CM_ "    prefix = 4 * (base >> 4)";
CM_ "    ext    = (prefix << 20) | (base << 8) | index        (id11 = base + index)";
CM_ "base = min(11-bit id of the family) - 1, index = 1..N inside the family. Decode with base = (ext >> 8) & 0xFFF, index = ext & 0xFF, id11 = base + index.";
CM_ "The prefix rule is verified on 129 extended ids with 0 mismatches: 85 in the GV60 captures and 44 in the Ioniq 6 capture.";
CM_ "This file lists the frames seen in ../Ioniq5_CAN/CAN_logs/other_cars/M-CAN_GV60_*.csv: all 85 remapped 29-bit frames, plus the plain 11-bit frames that ioniq5-2022.dbc / ev6-2024.dbc do not already define (those are NOT duplicated here - load those DBCs alongside this one). Where a remapped frame also exists on the Ioniq 5 / EV6 its name and signals are copied from ioniq5-2022.dbc / ev6-2024.dbc (name suffixed _GV60), so the copied comments describe the shared frame; otherwise the message only carries a raw DATA signal. ONE EXCEPTION: 0x0DC37F01 (11-bit 0x380) carries a raw DATA signal because the Ioniq 5 layout does not fit the CCU-hub payload - see its CM_.";
CM_ "DBC convention for extended frames: BO_ = 0x80000000 | ext, plus BA_ \"VFrameFormat\" BO_ <id> 1 (ExtendedCAN).";

BO_ 156 GV60_x0000009C: 8 Vector__XXX
