BO_ 2378399489 Climate_Temperature_GV60: 8 Vector__XXX
 SG_ DATA : 0|64@1+ (1,0) [0|0] "" Vector__XXX

CM_ BO_ 2378399489 "No signals: the Ioniq 5 0x380 layout used to be copied verbatim here and is WRONG for the CCU-hub payload, so it was removed in Oct 2026. The Ioniq 5 0x380 always has bytes 3-6 equal to each other (AD D7 FF 00 00 00 00 01, 73 DE 00 0C 0C 0C 0C 01, ...) while the GV60 payload is FC 60 52 24 41 02 00 00 - i.e. bytes 3-6 = 24 41 02 00, never equal - so Driver/Passenger/Rear_Temp_* decoded to 32.0 / 46.5 / 15.0 / Off degC in 2125/2125 frames.";
CM_ BO_ 2378399489 "This is not a GV60 quirk: the Ioniq 6 CCU-hub capture carries the same frame (0x0DC37F01, 1907 frames) as xx xx 92 24 41 02 00 00, i.e. the same 24 41 02 00 in bytes 3-6. Both CCU-hub cars therefore differ from the ICU-hub Ioniq 5 payload. Re-decode only from a capture taken while the climate setpoint is changed, and do not reuse the ioniq5-2022.dbc / ev6-2024.dbc 0x380 layout for CCU-hub captures.";
CM_ BO_ 2378399489 "GV60 29-bit 0x0DC37F01 = CCU-hub remap of 11-bit 0x380 (family base 0x37F, index 1), prefix 0x0DC = 4 * (0x37F >> 4). Observed payload (most common): FC 60 52 24 41 02 00 00.";

